# Documentation Audit Command

When the user says **"run documentation audit"**, **"documentation audit"**, or **"run doc audit"**:

## Execution mode (required)

Run in **Agent** mode with writes enabled—not Ask mode, not read-only subagents. The audit **must** create or update markdown under `docs/audits/`. **"No code changes"** means do not modify application or library source (for example under `app/`); it does **not** mean skip writing the report.

## What to do

1. Launch one subagent (generalPurpose) with read-only disabled and instruct it to follow `docs/process/documentation-audit-process.md`.
2. Require output report at `docs/audits/documentation/YYYY-MM-DD-documentation-audit.md` (or `YYYY-MM-DD-documentation-audit-N.md` if multiple runs on the same day).
3. Audit only. Do not make code changes.
4. After completion, summarize top findings and report location.

